PreK parent handbook for nathan 2627.pdf
# Source PDFs for the hub knowledge base — gated content (hub password,
# phone numbers); they live in Sanity as hubDocument files, not in git.
src/assets/*.pdf

# Camera original of the Twos/Threes class-pet photo. This repo is PUBLIC and
# the shot shows an identifiable child, while the page it appears on is behind
# the family login — so only the 900x506 derivative that actually renders
# (kit-the-kat-sm.webp) is committed. Keep the original locally if you need to
# regenerate at another size.
src/assets/photos/3L7A7778.jpg

# Real family data, produced by scripts/migrate-directory-to-kv.mjs.
# This repo is PUBLIC - committing it would be the same leak in a new store.
# Deliberately UNANCHORED: it matches a directory.json at any depth, so the
# rule still holds if someone runs the migration from another folder.
directory.json

# Real phone numbers, produced by scripts/migrate-teacher-phones-to-kv.mjs.
teacher-phones.json

# ...with one exception each, for the OBVIOUSLY FAKE test fixtures.
#
# The unanchored rules above silently swallowed these, and it went unnoticed
# because nothing ran the hub suite. seed-test-kv.mjs even claims in its header
# that the fixtures are "committed on purpose" — they were not committed at all,
# so the CI run would have had no directory to seed and every hub test would
# have failed against an empty one (found 2026-09-07).
#
# A negation weakens a rule that exists to stop a PII leak, so it does not stand
# alone: tests/fixtures.test.ts fails the build if either file grows anything
# that looks like a real address, phone number or email.
!tests/fixtures/directory.json
!tests/fixtures/teacher-phones.json

# Scratch dir for scripts/migrate-photos-to-r2.mjs. Holds real family photos.
.photo-migration/
